--- !u!114 &2795397989953867478
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: 'In real-life, cameras and the human brain attempt to compensate for strong color casts. This principle is called <b>white balancing.</b>


      It is especially important to balance Scenes with warm artificial lighting, because the corresponding lamps have a strong red color cast that might be unwanted depending on color accuracy or artistic requirements.


      In addition, white balancing allows you to adjust the overall temperature of the Scene to feel colder or warmer. This technique is used to fake a certain time of day (e.g. bluer for night, redder for sunset), and to convey certain emotions.'
--- !u!114 &5223278072220088301
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: "In this tutorial, you learned how <b>White Balance</b> can help you improve visual fidelity.\r\n\r\nFor more information about white balancing, you can check out this <a href=\"https://youtu.be/yqCHiZrgKzs?t=3749\">video</a> tutorial, or read more about it in the href=\"https://docs.unity3d.com/Packages/com.unity.render-pipelines.high-definition@latest/index.html?subfolder=/manual/Post-Processing-White-Balance.html\"<a>documentation.</a>\r\n\r\n<b>Note:</b> You do not need to save your changes in order to follow other tutorials.\r"
